-- chem/edgehol.hypercubical — the edge holonomy: the operator that moves flux through a link and so transfers one
-- unit of charge between the two vertices it joins, which the single-vertex magnetic loops provably cannot do
-- (chem/twovertex.hypercubical). An arc loop pushes a new innermost segment and leaves the edge's shared label
-- (beyond) fixed. The holonomy on the link edge multiplies that edge's own group element, so it shifts the shared
-- label itself: on bare ends, where beyond is the innermost label, it adds s to u's link-end label and −s to v's,
-- keeping the two ends matched (beyond(u.i) = −beyond(v.j)) at the new through-flux. Because on bare ends the label
-- is the charge-carrying innermost label, moving one unit of flux through the link raises u's net charge by one and
-- lowers v's by one: the edge holonomy transfers charge across the link, total charge conserved. This is the
-- operator an inter-vertex interaction is written in; its energy as a function of the link flux, and the force
-- between two charges from it, is the next step.
import "twovertex.hypercubical"

